STORE RULE
- Normal case (breaker closed, submit ok): store ONLY the POLL entry with jobId.
- SUBMIT entry is created ONLY when: breaker is OPEN, or the submit failed transiently/ambiguously.
- Permanent failure: store nothing, ERROR log.
- Final status: log + delete. Store = pending work only.

FAX FLOW - KAFKA STREAMS BASE DESIGN

TOPOLOGY
source topic -> filter (header PREFERENCE=FAX) -> FaxProcessor [store: fax-store]
non-FAX -> drop (counter only)

STORE  fax-store  (one store, changelog on)
key   = source topic-partition-offset (or MID)
value = stage            SUBMIT | POLL_JOB | POLL_DOCS
        mid, origin      for logs
        payload          original message (SUBMIT only, removed after send)
        firstSeenAt      record timestamp -> submit deadline
        attempt, ambiguousSends
        jobId, submittedAt -> poll deadline
        nextAttemptAt
        lastStatus, lastError
Store = pending work only. Final result -> log + delete entry.

PROCESS() - new message
1. breaker OPEN?          -> store SUBMIT (nextAttemptAt=now), no call
2. try submit:
   session cookie -> upload attachment -> sendJob (back to back, temp URL never stored)
   ok                     -> store POLL_JOB (jobId, nextAttemptAt=now+30s)
   transient              -> store SUBMIT (nextAttemptAt=now+backoff)
   sendJob outcome unknown-> store SUBMIT, ambiguousSends+1 (log POSSIBLE_DUPLICATE)
   permanent / bad data   -> ERROR log, store nothing
3. never throw for a classified failure (no thread kill)

PUNCTUATOR - WALL_CLOCK every 15-30s
1. breaker OPEN?          -> skip tick
2. collect due entries (nextAttemptAt <= now), close iterator before any HTTP call
3. order: SUBMIT first, then POLL, oldest first
4. loop until time budget (e.g. 60s) or call cap:
   SUBMIT:
     past submit deadline        -> ERROR SUBMIT_EXPIRED, delete
     ambiguousSends >= 2         -> ERROR SUBMISSION_UNCERTAIN, delete
     retry submit (same as process step 2), update entry right after the call
   POLL_JOB / POLL_DOCS:
     GET job (+ GET documents when job succeeded, same step)
     all docs Succeeded          -> INFO DELIVERED, delete
     Failed / Canceled           -> ERROR FAILED_FINAL_STATUS, delete
     pending / transient error   -> past poll deadline? ERROR FINAL_TIMEOUT, delete
                                    else nextAttemptAt = now + poll delay
     404 / 4xx                   -> 404 within 2m of submit: recheck; else ERROR, delete

SESSION (shared, thread-safe)
- login once, cache rf-session cookie, reuse for every call
- 401 / redirect / HTML page -> re-login once, repeat call
- fails again -> credential error -> auth breaker (no login for 10m, avoids account lockout)
- single-flight login (one thread logs in, others wait)

BACKOFF
retry: min(10m, 30s x 2^attempt) x random(0.7-1.3)
breaker OPEN wait: 60s -> 2m -> 4m ... cap 10m, jittered

ERROR CLASSES
not processed (retry):  connect refused/timeout, 408, 429, 503
ambiguous (retry, count): response timeout, reset, 500, 502, 504
permanent (no retry):   other 4xx, bad data, template/PDF error
2xx without jobId:      ERROR, never retry (would duplicate)

LIMITS / CONFIG
processing.guarantee  exactly_once_v2 (store + offset atomic)
transaction.timeout   5m
max.poll.interval     10m
punctuation budget    60s (must stay well under both)
submit deadline       e.g. 4h (business)
poll deadline         e.g. 2h (business)
max ambiguous sends   2

LOGGING
one line per outcome: outcome, MID, origin offset, stage, attempt, jobId, error
terminal = DELIVERED or ERROR; retries = INFO
metrics: store entries per stage, breaker state

DO NOT
- throw to retry (thread replace = no backoff + rebalance)
- keep final results in the store
- reset the Streams app while entries are pending
- retry sendJob blindly after a 2xx without jobId
